        {
          "_highlightResult": {
            "author": {
              "matchLevel": "none",
              "matchedWords": [],
              "value": "daliusd"
            },
            "comment_text": {
              "fullyHighlighted": false,
              "matchLevel": "full",
              "matchedWords": ["sqlite", ".", "org", "whentouse", ".", "html"],
              "value": "SQLite does not discourage using it for websites <a href=\"https://www.sqlite.org/whentouse.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.<em>sqlite.org</em>/<em>whentouse.html</em></a> . I use it for some low traffic web sites and I don't see any reason why I shouldn't. Benchmarking shows that my website can handle up to 400 req/s - that's not magic but it is far from my needs. As well it is convenient when memory usage of your web app is no more than 100Mb.<p>You should absolutely understand what you are doing but SQLite is good choice in many cases. Not everyone works on next Facebook."
            },
            "story_title": {
              "matchLevel": "none",
              "matchedWords": [],
              "value": "SQLite vs MySQL vs PostgreSQL"
            },
            "story_url": {
              "matchLevel": "none",
              "matchedWords": [],
              "value": "https://www.digitalocean.com/community/articles/sqlite-vs-mysql-vs-postgresql-a-comparison-of-relational-database-management-systems"
            }
          },
          "_tags": ["comment", "author_daliusd", "story_7432619"],
          "author": "daliusd",
          "children": [7434651],
          "comment_text": "SQLite does not discourage using it for websites <a href=\"https://www.sqlite.org/whentouse.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.sqlite.org&#x2F;whentouse.html</a> . I use it for some low traffic web sites and I don&#x27;t see any reason why I shouldn&#x27;t. Benchmarking shows that my website can handle up to 400 req&#x2F;s - that&#x27;s not magic but it is far from my needs. As well it is convenient when memory usage of your web app is no more than 100Mb.<p>You should absolutely understand what you are doing but SQLite is good choice in many cases. Not everyone works on next Facebook.",
          "created_at": "2014-03-20T07:08:41Z",
          "created_at_i": 1395299321,
          "objectID": "7434274",
          "parent_id": 7434076,
          "story_id": 7432619,
          "story_title": "SQLite vs MySQL vs PostgreSQL",
          "story_url": "https://www.digitalocean.com/community/articles/sqlite-vs-mysql-vs-postgresql-a-comparison-of-relational-database-management-systems",
